# Platform subdirs excluded from `git archive` output.
#
# The AUR tarball (and any deb-staging archive) is produced by
# `git archive <tag>`. Without export-ignore, these platform trees get
# swept into the Arch source tarball. export-ignore makes git archive
# omit them automatically -- self-maintaining, no per-ship vigilance.
#
# Add one line per platform subdir as it lands:
windows/ export-ignore

# Minified vendor JS, embedded raw via include_bytes! (windows/src/assets.rs)
# and compared byte-for-byte against what nginx serves on a Linux node.
# Without -text, a checkout with core.autocrlf=true (stock on Windows)
# rewrites this to CRLF on disk -- silent corruption at the SOURCE, before
# Rust even reads it, the same class of bug assets.rs's own lf() function
# exists to correct for index.html/cams.html (its doc comment: a checkout
# served 973 bytes larger than tina's, one \r per line, for no reason).
# text files get normalised in code; this one is marked binary instead,
# since include_bytes! has no equivalent runtime normalisation step to lf().
*.min.js -text
